{"id": "EUVD-2026-65224", "enisaUuid": "490f996c-bdb7-37eb-bc85-5f1c9e9113d4", "description": "GitPython versions before 3.1.59 contain an incomplete denylist in the unsafe_git_revision_options guard that omits --contents and -S options, allowing attackers to read arbitrary files by passing these options to Repo.blame(). Attackers can supply revision values like --contents=/etc/passwd to leak file contents through the blame result returned to the caller.", "datePublished": "2026-08-25T01:30:35", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-08T15:25:09", "baseScore": 7.1, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:H/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/gitpython-developers/GitPython/security/advisories/GHSA-5xxx-qhh7-9287", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/gitpython-before-arbitrary-file-read-via-repo-blame"], "aliases": ["PYSEC-2026-3788", "GHSA-89ff-m8wv-p99r", "CVE-2026-78678", "GHSA-5xxx-qhh7-9287"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.41, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "56e728e8-98bf-3eb7-83fe-eb2d8844531b", "product": {"name": "GitPython", "vendor": {"name": "gitpython-developers"}}, "product_version": "0 <3.1.59"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "22cfa5d8-8c16-3bcc-9c1b-ddfa58e222a2", "vendor": {"name": "gitpython-developers"}}], "isExploited": false}